      "title": "The Hidden Cost of Easy AI Wins \u2013 with Chris Caldwell of Concentrix",
      "summary": "AI deployments that look successful on internal dashboards can still drive up costs and push customers away once they scale beyond the pilot. In this episode, Chris Caldwell, President and CEO at Concentrix, unpacks why pilots built around the easiest use cases break down at scale, and why automating existing processes instead of redesigning the customer journey creates hidden costs. The conversation covers the behavioral signals that show when a customer needs a human, the role of real-time monitoring and quality assurance on AI interactions, and a sequence for moving to AI operations: brand promise, journey mapping, data and security readiness, and organizational change. This episode is sponsored by Concentrix Do you sell AI products or services? Emerj gives you access through trusted content and real conversations. Learn how leading AI brands like NVIDIA and Google Cloud work with Emerj to reach Fortune 500 AI buyers - download our media kit at: emerj.com/AD1",
